From a77d3ebf76cad823a460c42b3373a8001f2cb161 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sudharsan Veeravalli <svs@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 10:27:42 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] LTO with linker scripts, end-to-end.

"LTO with linker scripts" is a set of features that makes LTO interact in a more predictable way with linker scripts: the semantics of linker script rules are much closer to non-LTO semantics.

This includes all changes, end-to-end, required to enable LTO with linker scripts. All the changes are guarded under flags: a clang flag -flto-linker-scripts, and an lld flag --lto-linker-scripts.

Posting as one large patch so the whole design can be easily reviewed; I'll split into patches as appropriate once the approach is approved.

RFC: https://discourse.llvm.org/t/rfc-lto-lld-lto-with-linker-scripts-implemented/91089/1
